course: dictionary
lesson: 2189
title: Cosy: warm, safe and comfortable
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words paint a picture and a feeling at the same time. Cosy is one of them. «It feels so cosy that they forget they are outside.» The words around it show that the place feels warm and safe, so cosy means warm, comfortable and relaxed.
explain: Look for clues in the words near it. «A cosy bed nearby and a calm voice help it settle over a few nights.» A calm voice and a bed help something settle, so cosy must mean comfortable and restful. Check it by swapping in your meaning: «A warm, comfortable bed nearby» still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: Cosy can also describe a small place that feels friendly. «a cosy café» means a small, warm café where you feel at home. The same word can describe a feeling, a place or an object, so always look at the words around it.
explain: Cosy can also be a noun: a tea cosy is a cover that keeps a teapot warm. In the US the word is spelled cozy. When you read a word you do not know, first check the clues around it, then try your meaning in the sentence. If you are still not sure, use a dictionary.
fact: Cosy means warm, comfortable and safe, making you feel relaxed.
fact: Cosy can also mean small and friendly, like «a cosy café».
fact: A tea cosy is a cover that keeps a teapot warm.
fact: The US spelling is cozy. Comparative forms are cosier (more cosy) and cosiest (most cosy).
fact: Useful phrases are «nice and cosy», «cosy up» and «a cosy corner».
exercise: «It feels so cosy that they forget they are outside.» What does cosy mean here? | Very noisy and busy | Cold and wet | Dark and scary | *Warm, comfortable and relaxed
exercise: What is a tea cosy? | A kind of tea made from apples | A room where people drink tea | *A cover that keeps a teapot warm | A small cup for tea
exercise: «The shop was small and cosy, with a friendly owner.» What does cosy suggest about the shop? | Loud and busy | *Small and friendly | Huge and empty | Cold and grey
test: «A cosy bed nearby and a calm voice help it settle over a few nights.» What does cosy mean? | Wide and noisy | *Warm and comfortable | Hard and cold | Tidy and bare
test: Which word is the comparative form, meaning more cosy? | cosiness | cosiest | cosily | *cosier
exam: In «a normal flat with a cosy sofa», what does cosy tell you about the sofa? | *It is warm and comfortable | A sofa made of glass | A sofa that is too big for the room | A sofa that is outside
